# Root post-seal diagnostic read error

After the successful one-time control seal, a read-only PowerShell `Get-Content`
diagnostic requested the nonexistent `check_behavior-stdout.txt`. The tool call
therefore ended with exit 1 after printing the successful seal receipt. The
actual frozen checker's stdout file is `author-validation.json`; it was read on
the following diagnostic call and is a passing 5,210-cell verdict.

The seal helper itself exited 0 and produced the RO receipt
`i03-var03-root-seal-ssh-native-control_out1-20261007T233143347757Z-341e8041.json`,
SHA-256 `b67a98fd40ea6e4063caf6736a3e7f5cd4f03302ffa29fe8bef2efa3a28dd2ec`.
The native transport exited 0, all six native/checker stages exited 0, and all
25 original run files remained unchanged and RO. No native command was retried.

The path error is recorded from the tool transcript only. No original binary
stderr capture is claimed for that diagnostic PowerShell call.
